46-
47-```
48:.g-root                      → structural tokens (spacing, typography metrics, border radius)
49-.g-root_theme_light          → color tokens for the light theme
50-.g-root_theme_dark           → color tokens for the dark theme
51-```
--
102-
103-| Group                                             | Purpose                         | Examples                                                                 |
104-| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
105:| `--g-color-base-*`                                | Backgrounds & fills             | `base-background`, `base-brand`, `base-generic`, `base-danger-medium`    |
106:| `--g-color-text-*`                                | Text colors                     | `text-primary`, `text-secondary`, `text-hint`, `text-brand`, `text-link` |
107:| `--g-color-line-*`                                | Borders, dividers, underlines   | `line-generic`, `line-brand`, `line-focus`, `line-danger`                |
108-| `--g-color-sfx-*`                                 | Effects — shadows, veils, fades | `sfx-shadow`, `sfx-veil`, `sfx-fade`                                     |
109-| `--g-color-infographics-*` / `--g-color-scroll-*` | Charts, scrollbars              | `infographics-axis`, `scroll-handle`                                     |
110-
111-**Meaning conventions inside a group:**
112-
113-- **Statuses** — `info` (blue), `positive` (green), `warning` (yellow), `danger` (red),
114:  `utility` (purple), `misc` (cool grey), plus `brand`, `generic` and `neutral`.
115:- **Intensity** — `light` → `medium` → `heavy` go from subtle background fills to strong,
116-  filled surfaces. `heavy` fills are meant to carry contrasting (`*-contrast`) text on top.
117-- **Interaction** — a `-hover` suffix is the hover counterpart of the base token
118:  (e.g. `base-brand` / `base-brand-hover`).
119-- **Text hierarchy** — `text-primary` > `text-secondary` > `text-hint` (decreasing emphasis).
120-
121-```css
122:/* status background + matching text */
123-.alert-danger {
124:  background: var(--g-color-base-danger-light);
125-  color: var(--g-color-text-danger);
126-}
127-```
--
131-Branding is a subset of theming: override a small, curated set of variables to make UIKit look
132-like your product. In most cases you only need the accent color, fonts, and border radius.
133-
134:### Accent / brand color
135-
136:The accent color is what makes an app feel branded — action buttons, active controls, links, and
137:selection highlights. Override this group (per theme):
138-
139-| Variable                            | Used for                                          |
140-| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
141:| `--g-color-base-brand`              | Brand background (action button, active controls) |
142:| `--g-color-base-brand-hover`        | Hover background                                  |
143:| `--g-color-base-selection`          | Lighter brand tint (List/Table row selection)     |
144:| `--g-color-base-selection-hover`    | Hover of the selection tint                       |
145:| `--g-color-line-brand`              | Brand lines (active tab underline)                |
146:| `--g-color-text-brand`              | Brand text                                        |
147:| `--g-color-text-brand-heavy`        | Brand text over a background                      |
148:| `--g-color-text-brand-contrast`     | Text placed **on top of** a brand background      |
149:| `--g-color-text-link`               | Links                                             |
150:| `--g-color-text-link-hover`         | Hover of links                                    |
151:| `--g-color-text-link-visited`       | Visited links                                     |
152:| `--g-color-text-link-visited-hover` | Hover of visited links                            |
153-
154-```css
155-.g-root {
156:  --g-color-base-brand: rgb(117, 155, 255);
157:  --g-color-base-brand-hover: rgb(99, 143, 255);
158:  --g-color-base-selection: rgba(82, 130, 255, 0.05);
159:  --g-color-base-selection-hover: rgba(82, 130, 255, 0.1);
160:  --g-color-line-brand: rgb(117, 155, 255);
161:  --g-color-text-brand: rgb(117, 155, 255);
162:  --g-color-text-brand-contrast: rgb(255, 255, 255);
163:  --g-color-text-link: rgb(117, 155, 255);
164:  --g-color-text-link-hover: rgb(82, 130, 255);
165-}
166-```
167-
168:> Set these on the theme class (e.g. `.g-root_theme_light`) if the brand color should differ
169-> between light and dark; use `.g-root` for values shared by all themes.
